    <h2 id="about">About</h2>
    <p>
        This meetup is for those who work or aspire to work in fields like
        machine learning, data engineering, MLOps, visualization, and statistical modeling.
        We share real-world experiences about solving problems in these fields using open-source tools,
        including but not limited to Python and its libraries – users of R, Julia or other languages are welcome.
    </p>
    <p>
        We welcome speakers to talk about these tools and experiences using them, regardless of the level (beginner, intermediate, advanced are welcome).
        The usual talk is about half an hour long, but lightning talks of 5–10 minutes are great too!
        Occasionally we will include a debate! Come with a thought-provoking question or a hot take,
        and we'll set up a discussion where everyone can take part.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>Subscribe to our <a href="/events.ics">event calendar (iCal)</a> or the <a href="/feed.xml">Atom feed</a></li>
        <li>Join the conversation on <a href="https://helsinki-python.github.io/discord">the Helsinki Python Discord</a></li>
        <li>Contact us via email: <a href="mailto:pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com">pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com</a></li>
        <li>Follow us on the Fediverse: <a href="https://fosstodon.org/@pydata_helsinki" rel="me">@pydata_helsinki@fosstodon.org</a></li>
        <li>And on LinkedIn: <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/pydata-helsinki/" rel="me">PyData Helsinki</a></li>
        <li>If we succeed in recording talks (no promises), we'll put them up on <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@PyData_Helsinki" rel="me">YouTube</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="sponsors">Sponsors</h2>
    <ul>
        <li> We are always looking for sponsors who can provide us a venue and food and drinks for our meetup.
             In return, you can present your company or product at the meetup.
             See <a href="/for-companies/">information for companies</a> for details.
        </li>
        <li> The Meetup group is sponsored by <a href="https://numfocus.org/">NumFOCUS</a>: Promoting open code for better science.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="give-talk">Give a talk</h2>
    <p>
        We welcome speakers at any level, from beginner to advanced.
        Suitable topics include data science, AI, Python, Julia, R, etc.
        See <a href="/for-speakers/">information for speakers</a> for ideas and practicalities,
        and contact us by email or on the Discord server if you're interested.
    </p>
    {% set next_seeking = upcoming | rejectattr("status", "equalto", "cancelled") | selectattr("seeking_talks") | first %}
    {% if next_seeking %}
    <p>
        We are looking for more talks, in particular for
        <a href="/events/{{ next_seeking.slug }}/">{{ next_seeking.title }}</a>
        on <time datetime="{{ next_seeking.machine_date }}">{{ next_seeking.display_date }}</time>!
        Propose one on <a href="https://helsinki-python.github.io/discord">the Helsinki Python Discord</a>
        or by email to <a href="mailto:pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com">pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com</a>.
    </p>
    {% endif %}

    <h2 id="upcoming">Upcoming events</h2>
    <ul>
      {% for event in upcoming %}
      {% include "_event_list_item.html.j2" %}
      {% endfor %}
      <li>Please <a href="/for-companies/">offer your venue</a>
      by contacting us at <a href="mailto:pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com">pydata-helsinki-organisers@googlegroups.com</a>
      or on <a href="https://helsinki-python.github.io/discord">the Helsinki Python Discord</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Past events</h2>
    <ul>
      {% for event in past %}
